<article class="env-lemma" id="02SZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02SZ">Lemma <span data-tag="02SZ">115.23.5</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Chow Homology, Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$, $Y$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a proper morphism. Let $D \subset Y$ be an effective Cartier divisor. Assume $X$, $Y$ integral, $n = \dim _\delta (X) = \dim _\delta (Y)$ and $f$ dominant. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f_*[f^{-1}(D)]_{n - 1} = [R(X) : R(Y)] [D]_{n - 1}.  \]
</div>
  <p> In particular if $f$ is birational then $f_*[f^{-1}(D)]_{n - 1} = [D]_{n - 1}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from Chow Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02ST" data-tag="02ST">42.26.3</a> and the fact that $D$ is the zero scheme of the canonical section $1_ D$ of $\mathcal{O}_ X(D)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>